{"name":"Oxblood Red","hex":"#71383f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oxblood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark brownish-red colour.","The blood of an ox."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark brownish-red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oxblood"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oxblood","blocks":[{"text":"Oxblood or ox-blood is a dark shade of maroon, and is one of the darkest shades of red. It resembles burgundy, but has less purple and more dark brown hues. The French term sang-de-bœuf, or sang de bœuf, with the same meaning is used in various contexts in English, but especially in pottery, where sang de boeuf glaze in the color is a classic ceramic glaze in Chinese ceramics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Small_vase_MET_SLP1692-1_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Small_vase_MET_SLP1692-1_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxblood","wikidata":"Q2013559"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/500px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/1280px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg/500px-Unlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A pair of oxblood-colour Dr. Martens shoes","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUnlaced_Dr_Martens_Oxblood_Made_in_England_1461_shoes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Russell_Square_station.jpg/500px-Russell_Square_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Russell_Square_station.jpg/1280px-Russell_Square_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Russell_Square_station.jpg/500px-Russell_Square_station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Russell Square station, Piccadilly line, with the oxblood tile